{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches","id":1448259,"title":"Playable Fetches?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-11T14:03:38-07:00","id":1448259,"title":"Playable Fetches?","content":"So I have been reading Dark Eras 2, and I discovered a neat section on making Fetches playable. Unfortunately, while the section has good information about contract use, and roleplaying tips, it seems rather bare bones in other areas. So I\u2019ve got a few questions about it.<br /> <br /> 1) Does the Fetch use Wyrd or Azoth for it\u2019s power stat during the 7 wonders era? Or both?<br /> 2) Do fetches get the seeming bonus dot? It says their stats are equal to the Changelings, but is that before or after they are taken?<br /> 3) Can fetches use the gain the mantle of a court through court goodwill?<br /> 4) Can a playable Fetch buy Wyrd on their own, or does their Changeling have to do it?<br /> 5) If I wanted Echos to be purchasable, what should the cost be? <br /> 6) Should Fetches have Fetch only merits? Everything else playable seems to have merits only they can purchase?<br /> 6.5) Should some Changeling only merits be available to Fetches? Like Acute Senses?<br /> 7) Can a Changeling or their Fetch buy Parallel Lives before the Changeling has escaped?<br /> 8) Can a Fetch hedgespin?<br /> 8.5)Can a Fetch enact Paradigm Shifts?<br /> 9) Can a Fetch Portal, or Incite Bedlam?<br /> 10) Does a Fetch get the Seeming benefit if using Mimic Contract?<br /> 11) Can a Fetch participate in a Oaths if another Changeling actually does the magic?<br /> 12) Can a Fetch use Oneirmancy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T17:36:15-07:00","id":1448269,"title":"","content":"They use Wyrd, through since their not effected by disquiet the may be able to be friends with a Thong.<br /> <br /> Yes they should have special fetch merits,<br /> <br /> Since anyone can make a oath with a changling it should be possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T17:57:51-07:00","id":1448273,"title":"","content":"They probably shouldn\u2019t have Seeming-related stuff and Portalling... everything else seems accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T21:12:03-07:00","id":1448293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448269#post1448269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They use Wyrd, through since their not effected by disquiet the may be able to be friends with a Thong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess in 7 wonders, they don\u2019t use the pilgrimage system? Since they have no way to get vitriol?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448269#post1448269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they should have special fetch merits,</div> </div> </div> </div>If I attempted to make some, they should focus on mimicry, disguise, and entering the mirror world part of the hedge right? Or would those be echos? The Mirror contracts take away the obvious options.. maybe I could alter them, like Shard is a Fetch version of Elemental Weapon. Maybe I could have one where they talk to the mirror people?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448269#post1448269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since anyone can make a oath with a changling it should be possible</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree, but Oaths in 2e are strictly between Changelings, Huntsmen, and True Fae. Thing is the Wyrd counts the Fetch as the Changeling sometimes, so logically there should be some set of circumstances where the Wyrd accepts the Oath","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T21:12:47-07:00","id":1448294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448273#post1448273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably shouldn\u2019t have Seeming-related stuff and Portalling... everything else seems accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do they get that extra dot then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T21:22:58-07:00","id":1448295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448294#post1448294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do they get that extra dot then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say No by default, unless someone objects to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T07:08:45-07:00","id":1448584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448293#post1448293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess in 7 wonders, they don\u2019t use the pilgrimage system? Since they have no way to get vitriol?<br /> <br /> If I attempted to make some, they should focus on mimicry, disguise, and entering the mirror world part of the hedge right? Or would those be echos? The Mirror contracts take away the obvious options.. maybe I could alter them, like Shard is a Fetch version of Elemental Weapon. Maybe I could have one where they talk to the mirror people?<br /> <br /> I would agree, but Oaths in 2e are strictly between Changelings, Huntsmen, and True Fae. Thing is the Wyrd counts the Fetch as the Changeling sometimes, so logically there should be some set of circumstances where the Wyrd accepts the Oath</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait really? Why did they change that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T10:49:43-07:00","id":1448601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448584#post1448584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait really? Why did they change that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm qualified to hazard a guess, but the wording is rather specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling the Lost Second Edition, pg 212</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An oath between two changelings is at once a commonplace and special occurrence. Oaths are a kind of <br /> currency to the Lost, because all of them understand that <br /> any temporal reward could become meaningless at any <br /> moment. When everything falls apart, all a changeling <br /> has is her word, and she doesn\u2019t give that away lightly. If <br /> two (or more) changelings are willing to exchange oaths, <br /> they know and the Wyrd knows that they are serious about their feelings. <br /> <b>Changelings, Huntsmen, and the True Fae are the <br /> only beings that can swear oaths, and Huntsmen cannot <br /> swear oaths to each other.</b> <i>Human beings and other non-fae creatures can make bargains with the Lost, but these <br /> are defined by what the bargaining parties will do, not <br /> what they feel.</i> Oaths are sworn with heart, soul, blood, <br /> and Wyrd. The actions the swearer takes demonstrate <br /> whether she follows or violates an oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are more types of Pledges, but Oaths are the one with the most power. I don't know why it changed so you can't perform this with mortals or other supernatural creatures, but I think Hobgoblins and Fetches should be able to swear oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T20:38:56-07:00","id":1448650,"title":"","content":"Are not Goblins made out of Wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T21:54:34-07:00","id":1448655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448601#post1448601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are more types of Pledges, but Oaths are the one with the most power. I don't know why it changed so you can't perform this with mortals or other supernatural creatures, but I think Hobgoblins and Fetches should be able to swear oaths.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448650#post1448650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are not Goblins made out of Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hobgoblins are made out of whatever they're made out of, which can include a number of things that absolutely aren't the Wyrd. Like humans.<br /> <br /> They also can't learn Court or Royal Arcadian Contracts and handle their dealmaking through Sealings and the exchange of Goblin Debt for goods and services.<br /> <br /> An Oath involves two parties with a direct relation to something of Arcadia. Huntsmen pre-date the rise of Contracts but serve as vessels for the Fae's desires; changelings have some remnant of a human soul and were transformed utterly in Faerie itself; fae-touched leverage a promise with a changeling to open up their partial connection to the Wyrd by exposure to Faerie's borderland on the way there; and the Gentry are, of course, the architects of the system and its primary beneficiaries who go harder into it than anyone else.<br /> <br /> The consequences of an Oath are largely limited to changelings in their specific relevance \u2014 if you want to establish consequences for breaking your word, literally every type of pledge does that and the most prosaic one is a universal ability of the fae; if you want an agreement to help each other, that's what Bargains are for and they're where the &quot;using this in crossover can cause of weird side-effects&quot; stuff lives; if you want to make a deal that redefines its participants, you're out of luck for anything that isn't Of Faerie or upholding an old promise with something in that vein, because fetches are spoken for and hobgoblins only seem like they aren't.<br /> <br /> Oaths are powerful because they have stakes for the Lost and their other parties. Mortals don't have Contracts that can fizzle out or a secret face that changelings have innate special insight into or Clarity attacks to worsen, so the Oathbreaker Condition doesn't have any real purchase to make on their actions, either.<br /> <br /> If what you're instead wondering is why pledges changed to mostly grant boons that you actually had access to, it may have something to do with the multiple times people asked why every changeling wasn't filthy rich and living on easy street despite 1e's implication that the Lost tend to use looser more-exploitable language in pledgecrafting with mortals. There's not much point in being a game about being a fugitive trying to rebuild your life while sticking to a consistent locale and working with magic that tries to keep the books balanced if everyone can wordsmith their way to comfort at character creation; not for nothing does Demon use its similar system with an Integrity analogue that lets them cut and run with increasing frequency; not for nothing does Deviant's power structure include an explicit tagging system for &quot;this game element will attract unwanted attention to you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T11:11:00-07:00","id":1448707,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks Satchel. That was a excellent explanation. <br /> <br /> If I wanted Fetches to get in on the Pledge business, would that power be a echo or a merit? If I wanted a Fetch to gain the seeming benefits from it\u2019s Changeling, that would be a echo? Maybe a merit based on that concept for the seeming power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T11:30:12-07:00","id":1448709,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Fetches are perfectly playable now in 2e. That said, I\u2019m super excited to see the expanded rules for Fetches in Kith &amp; Kin, they have always been one of my favorite aspects of Changeling!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"ran