\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448655#post1448655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If what you're instead wondering is why pledges changed to mostly grant boons that you actually had access to, it may have something to do with the multiple times people asked why every changeling wasn't filthy rich and living on easy street despite 1e's implication that the Lost tend to use looser more-exploitable language in pledgecrafting with mortals. There's not much point in being a game about being a fugitive trying to rebuild your life while sticking to a consistent locale and working with magic that tries to keep the books balanced if everyone can wordsmith their way to comfort at character creation; not for nothing does Demon use its similar system with an Integrity analogue that lets them cut and run with increasing frequency; not for nothing does Deviant's power structure include an explicit tagging system for &quot;this game element will attract unwanted attention to you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to reply on this but it was worth its own thread so I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1449175-what-s-wrong-with-1e-pledges-should-i-use-them\">a new one</a><br /> <br /> Also, I had a question about Fetch Touchstones I posted <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1449174#post1449174\">on the Ask a Simple Question thread</a> which may be relevant to this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T07:24:32-07:00","id":1449188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1448273#post1448273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably shouldn\u2019t have Seeming-related stuff and Portalling... everything else seems accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they lack Clarity, they also cannot use Kenning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T01:33:34-07:00","id":1449632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches#post1448259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have been reading Dark Eras 2, and I discovered a neat section on making Fetches playable. Unfortunately, while the section has good information about contract use, and roleplaying tips, it seems rather bare bones in other areas. So I\u2019ve got a few questions about it.<br /> <br /> 1) Does the Fetch use Wyrd or Azoth for it\u2019s power stat during the 7 wonders era? Or both?<br /> 2) Do fetches get the seeming bonus dot? It says their stats are equal to the Changelings, but is that before or after they are taken?<br /> 3) Can fetches use the gain the mantle of a court through court goodwill?<br /> 4) Can a playable Fetch buy Wyrd on their own, or does their Changeling have to do it?<br /> 5) If I wanted Echos to be purchasable, what should the cost be?<br /> 6) Should Fetches have Fetch only merits? Everything else playable seems to have merits only they can purchase?<br /> 6.5) Should some Changeling only merits be available to Fetches? Like Acute Senses?<br /> 7) Can a Changeling or their Fetch buy Parallel Lives before the Changeling has escaped?<br /> 8) Can a Fetch hedgespin?<br /> 8.5)Can a Fetch enact Paradigm Shifts?<br /> 9) Can a Fetch Portal, or Incite Bedlam?<br /> 10) Does a Fetch get the Seeming benefit if using Mimic Contract?<br /> 11) Can a Fetch participate in a Oaths if another Changeling actually does the magic?<br /> 12) Can a Fetch use Oneirmancy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooo, I can dig in to this a bit, since I'm running a game where the players are Fetches.<br /> <br /> 1) Fetch should use Wyrd. They are beings of Glamour, after all, and while there's a LOT of cool stuff you can add to a Fetch game from Promethean, Fetch are ultimately different beings. You might consider some crossover, though -- I have some Pandorans running around in my game that react to both Wyrd and Azoth, because they were created by one of the Gentry trying his hand at wielding The Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> 2) When I worked up my Fetch rules, I created six splats to parallel Seemings. The splats dealt with what the Fetch was constructed out of, and how that influenced their lives. Each of these &quot;Bundles,&quot; as I called them, gave a Fetch a different bonus (though I used the whole grid of Power/Finesse/Resistance and Mental/Physical/Social to devide up the bonuses). The Fetch were not required to take a Bundle that had anything to do with their Changeling Counterpart's Seeming.<br /> <br /> 3) I'd allow it, since otherwise they're gimped if they have Mimic Contract but their changeling counterpart uses a lot of Court Contracts over Arcadian ones.<br /> <br /> 4) I'd allow the <i>players</i> to make such an expenditure, sure. Whether or not it represents the Changeling increasing their Wyrd and the Fetch gaining it by proxy or whether Fetch themselves can raise it is immaterial -- I view advancement as a Player-level choice, not a Character-level one. But that's just how <i>I</i> handle it.<br /> <br /> 5) I use one Experience per dot of Wyrd requirement -- a Wyrd 1 Echo costs 1 Experience, while a Wyrd 2 Echo costs 2, etc. I also packaged a Favored Echo into the Bundles I created, allowing each Bundle to have signature strengths. I imported a lot of Echoes from Autumn Nightmares (cleaned up for 2e) and made a few of my own, and my players also submitted ideas for Echoes that I worked the mechanics out for. This, of course, if just how I do things...my recommendation is to keep the price in line with other supernatural abilities, which tend to cost between 2 and 4 Experiences in most of the splats.<br /> <br /> 6) I think so. I swiped a bunch of Promethean Merits for my game, allowed Fetch to take some Supernatural Merits normally reserved strictly for mortals (Aura Sense, Omen Sensitivity, and Object Reading), as well as came up with a series of Merits based on the idea of &quot;Fetch Catches&quot; from Autumn Nightmares.<br /> <br /> 6.5) Again, I think so, and allow Merits with some caveats (some have prerequisites of requiring certain Echoes, most notably anything related to entering or navigating The Hedge).<br /> <br /> 7) I see nothing but interesting story developments from that, so I'd allow it as an ST. It will fuck up the Fetch's life no end to be that tied to their Changeling even before their escape.<br /> <br /> 8) I allow it, assuming the Fetch can get into the Hedge in the first place. But I bundled the ability to Hedgespin into the Enter The Hedge Echo, so it's not a universal ability among Fetch.<br /> <br /> 9) Enter The Hedge is already an Echo that Fetch can take if they want. So some Fetch can Portal. I don't allow them to have the &quot;slip free of any binding&quot; ability, though; that's strictly a Changeling ability. Likewise, I have an Echo that allows Fetch to incite Bedlam. I've also swiped some Promethean Bestowments to use as Echoes (most notably Ephemeral Flesh, Inscription, The Soul Is In The Software, and Spare Parts).<br /> <br /> 10) Yes. They gain the Contract exactly as their Counterpart knows it. I view buying new Seeming Abilities the same way I do buying Wyrd -- that's a Player-Level choice, and you can justify it in the narrative however you like.<br /> <br /> 11) Not so much. I have an Echo that allows Fetch to use Sealing, but not Oaths. I use the 1e version of Pledgecrafting in my game as a supplement, but I haven't given the Fetches the ability to do more than Sealing thus far.<br /> <br /> 12) Again, I bundled this ability into an Echo that allowed Fetch to enter dreams if they can get into the Hedge. I didn't make the ability universal for all Fetches.<br /> <br /> If you are curious, I wrote out a lot of my Fetch Player Creation rules <a href=\"https://r.rpol.net/display.cgi?gi=74627&amp;ti=3&amp;date=1600922933\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. This is the main Request To Join thread for my game, which includes all the player options and rules I'm using that aren't in the base Changeling book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T08:39:02-07:00","id":1449660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oooo, I can dig in to this a bit, since I'm running a game where the players are Fetches.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for answering.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Fetch should use Wyrd. They are beings of Glamour, after all, and while there's a LOT of cool stuff you can add to a Fetch game from Promethean, Fetch are ultimately different beings. You might consider some crossover, though -- I have some Pandorans running around in my game that react to both Wyrd and Azoth, because they were created by one of the Gentry trying his hand at wielding The Divine Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div> ... that sounds amazing. I always plan on some crossover, Out of Context problems seems like a good way to throw players for a loop, and make a interesting narrative.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) When I worked up my Fetch rules, I created six splats to parallel Seemings. The splats dealt with what the Fetch was constructed out of, and how that influenced their lives. Each of these &quot;Bundles,&quot; as I called them, gave a Fetch a different bonus (though I used the whole grid of Power/Finesse/Resistance and Mental/Physical/Social to devide up the bonuses). The Fetch were not required to take a Bundle that had anything to do with their Changeling Counterpart's Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see. I did find it odd that Changelings get a bonus dot and Fetches don\u2019t, because it seems even a fresh out of the hedge Changeling can reasonably murder their Fetch, because the Changeling is batter from a numbers standpoint in every way. The Bundles wouldn\u2019t alleviate that, but they would give it a new and interesting shape.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I'd allow it, since otherwise they're gimped if they have Mimic Contract but their changeling counterpart uses a lot of Court Contracts over Arcadian ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a good point. Court Goodwill is already a good Merit without the Mantle, so I wasn\u2019t sure if it would.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) I'd allow the <i>players</i> to make such an expenditure, sure. Whether or not it represents the Changeling increasing their Wyrd and the Fetch gaining it by proxy or whether Fetch themselves can raise it is immaterial -- I view advancement as a Player-level choice, not a Character-level one. But that's just how <i>I</i> handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div> So if a Changeling is still in Arcadia, and their Wyrd raises, would their Keeper be likely to notice? You know, depending on the Keeper, and depending on the relationship between them and the Changeling.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) I use one Experience per dot of Wyrd requirement -- a Wyrd 1 Echo costs 1 Experience, while a Wyrd 2 Echo costs 2, etc. I also packaged a Favored Echo into the Bundles I created, allowing each Bundle to have signature strengths. I imported a lot of Echoes from Autumn Nightmares (cleaned up for 2e) and made a few of my own, and my players also submitted ideas for Echoes that I worked the mechanics out for. This, of course, if just how I do things...my recommendation is to keep the price in line with other supernatural abilities, which tend to cost between 2 and 4 Experiences in most of the splats.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool. That\u2019s a good system I feel.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) I think so. I swiped a bunch of Promethean Merits for my game, allowed Fetch to take some Supernatural Merits normally reserved strictly for mortals (Aura Sense, Omen Sensitivity, and Object Reading), as well as came up with a series of Merits based on the idea of &quot;Fetch Catches&quot; from Autumn Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see. I was wondering about a series of Merits or Echos that allowed contact with the Mirror People, maybe even using Mirrors as Hedgegates.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6.5) Again, I think so, and allow Merits with some caveats (some have prerequisites of requiring certain Echoes, most notably anything related to entering or navigating The Hedge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) I see nothing but interesting story developments from that, so I'd allow it as an ST. It will fuck up the Fetch's life no end to be that tied to their Changeling even before their escape.</div> </div> </div> </div> I asked because I had thought of playing a Fetch that after a really bad, but mostly normal day, that while looking into a mirror, the first mind vision comes, and all of my illusions are shattered. The vision would be of their Durance, because they hadn\u2019t escaped. Of course that only works if you can develop Parallel Lives before the escape.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8) I allow it, assuming the Fetch can get into the Hedge in the first place. But I bundled the ability to Hedgespin into the Enter The Hedge Echo, so it's not a universal ability among Fetch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems sensible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9) Enter The Hedge is already an Echo that Fetch can take if they want. So some Fetch can Portal. I don't allow them to have the &quot;slip free of any binding&quot; ability, though; that's strictly a Changeling ability. Likewise, I have an Echo that allows Fetch to incite Bedlam. I've also swiped some Promethean Bestowments to use as Echoes (most notably Ephemeral Flesh, Inscription, The Soul Is In The Software, and Spare Parts).</div> </div> </div> </div> Well I need Promethean then. Those Bestowments sound delightful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10) Yes. They gain the Contract exactly as their Counterpart knows it. I view buying new Seeming Abilities the same way I do buying Wyrd -- that's a Player-Level choice, and you can justify it in the narrative however you like.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that\u2019s very interesting. I liked seeming bonuses, they help make the Contracts feel special and different for every character.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11) Not so much. I have an Echo that allows Fetch to use Sealing, but not Oaths. I use the 1e version of Pledgecrafting in my game as a supplement, but I haven't given the Fetches the ability to do more than Sealing thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I will trust your judgment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12) Again, I bundled this ability into an Echo that allowed Fetch to enter dreams if they can get into the Hedge. I didn't make the ability universal for all Fetches.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sensible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are curious, I wrote out a lot of my Fetch Player Creation rules <a href=\"https://r.rpol.net/display.cgi?gi=74627&amp;ti=3&amp;date=1600922933\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. This is the main Request To Join thread for my game, which includes all the player options and rules I'm using that aren't in the base Changeling book.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you thank you thank you. I like Fetches, but I don\u2019t have the time anymore to spend on making things. I will happily read this and if I ever get to do a game, use it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T08:56:44-07:00","id":1449665,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25851_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25851\" data-vbnamecard=\"25851\">TheStray7</a> If I want to play something similar to the Plain Doll from Bloodborne, or a Oversized Windup toy, that\u2019s a Mannequien right? Edit: Upon further reflection, I think the doll might be a Curio, because she bleeds some white substance, her tears are gemstones or solid blood, she seemingly has a human face, but a Mannequiens fingers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-26-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T10:40:42-07:00","id":1449671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449660#post1449660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... that sounds amazing. I always plan on some crossover, Out of Context problems seems like a good way to throw players for a loop, and make a interesting narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. In the game I'm running, I'm using a lot of material from Promethean, Demon, and Geist in addition to all the Changeling stuff. It's fun mixing things in...both Demons and Prometheans have themes that dovetail nicely with Changeling in interesting ways, especially from the &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TomatoInTheMirror\" target=\"_blank\">Tomato in the mirror</a>&quot; game that this one is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. I did find it odd that Changelings get a bonus dot and Fetches don\u2019t, because it seems even a fresh out of the hedge Changeling can reasonably murder their Fetch, because the Changeling is batter from a numbers standpoint in every way. The Bundles wouldn\u2019t alleviate that, but they would give it a new and interesting shape. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Fetches are still an underdog here, but Fetches aren't supposed to be a physical threat to their changelings so much as an emotional/societal one. The Fetch has all the connections to the regular, mundane world of humans that the Changeling lacks, and their very existence can cause Changelings to question their sanity. And killing a Fetch, which is a sentient, self-aware creature (often times completely innocent of any real wrongdoing and possibly not even aware of what it is) is still murder. The reason i wanted to run this game to begin with was to explore that sort of perspective flip horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if a Changeling is still in Arcadia, and their Wyrd raises, would their Keeper be likely to notice? You know, depending on the Keeper, and depending on the relationship between them and the Changeling. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. It would probably make it easier to escape, though, and I had all the characters in this game start at Wyrd 2 strictly for gameplay reasons rather than narrative ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. I was wondering about a series of Merits or Echos that allowed contact with the Mirror People, maybe even using Mirrors as Hedgegates </div> </div> </div>I've certainly considered it, and with the existence of the Mirage Bundle in my game, playing <i>as</i> a Mirror Person is possible. I haven't implemented such a system yet, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I asked because I had thought of playing a Fetch that after a really bad, but mostly normal day, that while looking into a mirror, the first mind vision comes, and all of my illusions are shattered. The vision would be of their Durance, because they hadn\u2019t escaped. Of course that only works if you can develop Parallel Lives before the escape. </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that if something sounds like it would make for an interesting story, I'd be willing to bend the lore to accommodate it. However, the Fetch might not realize they're a Fetch, even after this. Unless gaining the merit explicitly reveals the situation to them, they're likely to think they just have some horrible tie to a monster on the other side of the mirror, one that <i>knows</i> about them. Humans tend to be good at self-delusional rationalization to protect their core identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I need Promethean then. Those Bestowments sound delightful. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd had this idea bouncing in my brain for years, but it wasn't until I picked up Promethean that it all sort of clicked together for me.<br /> <br /> As a brief overview:<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Flesh allows the character to see into and interact with beings in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Inscription is a secret word of phrase that's been written on the character that the character can invoke to renew their sense of self or purpose, allowing them to use their magic fuel (Pyros in the Promethean's case, and Glamour in the Fetch's) to be spent like a point of Willpower on one of three skills. They can only do this once per skill per Chapter, but it's still really handy as it's easier to regain magic fuel than Willpower in a lot of cases.<br /> <br /> The Soul Is In The Software allows the character to separate parts of themselves into smaller bits to run around and do things. It's mostly useful for separating a piece of yourself to do recon or to save yourself from immanent death (the separated body part can grow into a new body if the original one is killed).<br /> <br /> Spare Parts allows a character to replace their body parts with fresh ones, allowing them to switch around their stats or even heal damage. I allow Fetches to use things other than flesh parts for this -- each Fetch has a &quot;primary element&quot; they're composed of (wood, plastic, mud, bones, non-iron metal, etc.) that they can swallow down to heal damage (this gives them a way of speeding up recovery between fights, and is mostly a gameplay consideration) -- Spare Parts for them works with their primary element, and is basically meant to be an extension of the ability taken to its logical conclusion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, that\u2019s very interesting. I liked seeming bonuses, they help make the Contracts feel special and different for every character. </div> </div> </div>I liked them so much I gave Echoes similar benefits...different types of Fetches can make use of their Echoes in different ways. Since I'm just one person with only so much creative energy, I could only come up with so many Echoes at a given Wyrd rating -- benefits like these allowed for more character customization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright. I will trust your judgment. </div> </div> </div>I want to stress that this was stuff I did that made sense for the sort of game I wanted to run. Your mileage may vary and you might decide to go deeper into that than I wanted to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> thank you thank you thank you. I like Fetches, but I don\u2019t have the time anymore to spend on making things. I will happily read this and if I ever get to do a game, use it. </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I hope it's useful. I'm interested to see how Kith &amp; Kin deals with playable Fetches, as I suspect I may incorporate some ideas from it into my little homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T10:45:28-07:00","id":1449672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449665#post1449665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25851_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25851\" data-vbnamecard=\"25851\">TheStray7</a> If I want to play something similar to the Plain Doll from Bloodborne, or a Oversized Windup toy, that\u2019s a Mannequien right? Edit: Upon further reflection, I think the doll might be a Curio, because she bleeds some white substance, her tears are gemstones or solid blood, she seemingly has a human face, but a Mannequiens fingers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mannequin, Curio, or Effigy, likely. Maybe Doppelganger if the Gentry that created them used Arcadian or Hedge materials to make them. The Bundles are not hard-and-fast divisions and it's more a function of what you, as a player or storyteller, want to emphasize about their creation. The Gentry aren't picky when it comes to ingredients for Fetches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T22:30:21-07:00","id":1449758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. In the game I'm running, I'm using a lot of material from Promethean, Demon, and Geist in addition to all the Changeling stuff. It's fun mixing things in...both Demons and Prometheans have themes that dovetail nicely with Changeling in interesting ways, especially from the &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TomatoInTheMirror\" target=\"_blank\">Tomato in the mirror</a>&quot; game that this one is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Geist is also good for Ship of Theseus type questions. Maybe Deviant as a counter point?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Fetches are still an underdog here, but Fetches aren't supposed to be a physical threat to their changelings so much as an emotional/societal one. The Fetch has all the connections to the regular, mundane world of humans that the Changeling lacks, and their very existence can cause Changelings to question their sanity. And killing a Fetch, which is a sentient, self-aware creature (often times completely innocent of any real wrongdoing and possibly not even aware of what it is) is still murder. The reason i wanted to run this game to begin with was to explore that sort of perspective flip horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a philosophical standpoint, is either the Changeling or the Fetch really the original? I mean, the Changeling is missing huge chunks of Original, and so is the Fetch. Guess it\u2019s a Ship of Theseus question, which considering my answer to that problem means both are the Original and Not at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea. It would probably make it easier to escape, though, and I had all the characters in this game start at Wyrd 2 strictly for gameplay reasons rather than narrative ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, that\u2019s like starting at level 5 for d&amp;d right? Still a nice start, but far enough into power that it\u2019s not boring? (D&amp;D 5e is the only thing my group does.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've certainly considered it, and with the existence of the Mirage Bundle in my game, playing <i>as</i> a Mirror Person is possible. I haven't implemented such a system yet, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe something similar to summoning the reflection of the Meket, and the Hob Kin merit? From what I understand, Mirror People aren\u2019t Hobs, and might be sympathetic to another shadow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that if something sounds like it would make for an interesting story, I'd be willing to bend the lore to accommodate it. However, the Fetch might not realize they're a Fetch, even after this. Unless gaining the merit explicitly reveals the situation to them, they're likely to think they just have some horrible tie to a monster on the other side of the mirror, one that <i>knows</i> about them. Humans tend to be good at self-delusional rationalization to protect their core identity.</div> </div> </div> </div> See, that\u2019s where I have problems understanding how one could deny this. I mean, this is contact with their Changeling, right? Maybe they don\u2019t realize right away who each other are, and their connection but this in my mind is enough to make the Fetch see through their Mask for the first time. Add that the Fetch can and sometimes is forced to take part in the Durance, and can feel the suffering Changeling endures, denying it seems like a express lane down to crazy town. Actually, I guess \u201cI went insane and occasionally see things\u201d is easier to believe than \u201cFairies kidnapped me and made a almost perfect clone of me mentally, and I\u2019m the clone\u201d. Still feels weird. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd had this idea bouncing in my brain for years, but it wasn't until I picked up Promethean that it all sort of clicked together for me.<br /> <br /> As a brief overview:<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Flesh allows the character to see into and interact with beings in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Inscription is a secret word of phrase that's been written on the character that the character can invoke to renew their sense of self or purpose, allowing them to use their magic fuel (Pyros in the Promethean's case, and Glamour in the Fetch's) to be spent like a point of Willpower on one of three skills. They can only do this once per skill per Chapter, but it's still really handy as it's easier to regain magic fuel than Willpower in a lot of cases.<br /> <br /> The Soul Is In The Software allows the character to separate parts of themselves into smaller bits to run around and do things. It's mostly useful for separating a piece of yourself to do recon or to save yourself from immanent death (the separated body part can grow into a new body if the original one is killed).<br /> <br /> Spare Parts allows a character to replace their body parts with fresh ones, allowing them to switch around their stats or even heal damage. I allow Fetches to use things other than flesh parts for this -- each Fetch has a &quot;primary element&quot; they're composed of (wood, plastic, mud, bones, non-iron metal, etc.) that they can swallow down to heal damage (this gives them a way of speeding up recovery between fights, and is mostly a gameplay consideration) -- Spare Parts for them works with their primary element, and is basically meant to be an extension of the ability taken to its logical conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div> These are neat, and I like what you did with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked them so much I gave Echoes similar benefits...different types of Fetches can make use of their Echoes in different ways. Since I'm just one person with only so much creative energy, I could only come up with so many Echoes at a given Wyrd rating -- benefits like these allowed for more character customization.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, these are neat and I like what you did with them. I have one question though, on Lighter than a Feather Mannequin bonus, what does higher than 5 dots in Parkour do? Because I think Wyrd 10 Parkour need to happen at some point. For reasons. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to stress that this was stuff I did that made sense for the sort of game I wanted to run. Your mileage may vary and you might decide to go deeper into that than I wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just think I would like some of the deeper Pledges and Oaths available, even if they are way harder to obtain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449671#post1449671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I hope it's useful. I'm interested to see how Kith &amp; Kin deals with playable Fetches, as I suspect I may incorporate some ideas from it into my little homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well it entertained me,and I\u2019m going to use it if I can. I count that as useful. I can\u2019t wait for Kith &amp; Kin, all signs point to it being amazing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T23:59:38-07:00","id":1449766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449758#post1449758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Geist is also good for Ship of Theseus type questions. Maybe Deviant as a counter point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever Deviant flipping releases, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a philosophical standpoint, is either the Changeling or the Fetch really the original? I mean, the Changeling is missing huge chunks of Original, and so is the Fetch. Guess it\u2019s a Ship of Theseus question, which considering my answer to that problem means both are the Original and Not at the same time. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the <i>small</i> questions. I do think that's been brought up in in-game conversation, though, so it's something worth pondering. Also worth pondering is possibly drawing in the Sworn Ship of Theseus from The Contagion Chronicles, since they're most concerned about that line of thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, that\u2019s like starting at level 5 for d&amp;d right? Still a nice start, but far enough into power that it\u2019s not boring? (D&amp;D 5e is the only thing my group does.) </div> </div> </div>I liken it more to level 3, but yes, that's the sort of thing I'm aiming for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe something similar to summoning the reflection of the Meket, and the Hob Kin merit? From what I understand, Mirror People aren\u2019t Hobs, and might be sympathetic to another shadow. </div> </div> </div>Cool, that's a neat idea, thanks. Going to have to dig out my copy of V:tR to look up the specifics. As for Hob Kin, I have an NPC that has a variant that's tied to the Mirror People, as I was planning on using them at some point. So that's not a terrible stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, that\u2019s where I have problems understanding how one could deny this. I mean, this is contact with their Changeling, right? Maybe they don\u2019t realize right away who each other are, and their connection but this in my mind is enough to make the Fetch see through their Mask for the first time. Add that the Fetch can and sometimes is forced to take part in the Durance, and can feel the suffering Changeling endures, denying it seems like a express lane down to crazy town. Actually, I guess \u201cI went insane and occasionally see things\u201d is easier to believe than \u201cFairies kidnapped me and made a almost perfect clone of me mentally, and I\u2019m the clone\u201d. Still feels weird. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_dissonance\" target=\"_blank\">Cognitive Dissonance</a> is a helluva drug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are neat, and I like what you did with them. </div> </div> </div>Thank you. This was a ton of work to put together, even just swiping stuff from other sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, these are neat and I like what you did with them. I have one question though, on Lighter than a Feather Mannequin bonus, what does higher than 5 dots in Parkour do? Because I think Wyrd 10 Parkour need to happen at some point. For reasons. </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, nothing, since Merits can't get beyond 5 dots. With Parkour 5 and a few Steed Contracts you're <i>already</i> doing plenty of wuxia-level nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just think I would like some of the deeper Pledges and Oaths available, even if they are way harder to obtain. </div> </div> </div>Noted. I'll probably revisit that when I get my attention on filling out the higher-Wyrd Echoes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well it entertained me, and I\u2019m going to use it if I can. I count that as useful. I can\u2019t wait for Kith &amp; Kin, all signs point to it being amazing. </div> </div> </div>I'm waiting on that, The Deviant book, Hunter 2e...lots of stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T00:50:22-07:00","id":1449771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449758#post1449758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a philosophical standpoint, is either the Changeling or the Fetch really the original? I mean, the Changeling is missing huge chunks of Original, and so is the Fetch. Guess it\u2019s a Ship of Theseus question, which considering my answer to that problem means both are the Original and Not at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ship of Theseus thought experiment is about the original having its components replaced piece by piece until nothing of the original exists anymore, which means there's still continuity between the original ship and the new ship. The fetch is made wholesale as a copy and put into the original's place, with only a single piece of the original used in their creation.<br /> Now, the changeling might also not be considered the original since they are reshaped utterly by their Durance.<br /> <br /> The interesting question comes from moral philosophy: Does the changeling still have any claim on their old life if another thinking being is already in possession of it and has lived it for a significant amount of time? Is it okay to try to resume the fetch's relationships even though those people have built such relationships with the fetch instead of the changeling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T01:55:49-07:00","id":1449774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449771#post1449771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ship of Theseus thought experiment is about the original having its components replaced piece by piece until nothing of the original exists anymore, which means there's still continuity between the original ship and the new ship. The fetch is made wholesale as a copy and put into the original's place, with only a single piece of the original used in their creation.<br /> Now, the changeling might also not be considered the original since they are reshaped utterly by their Durance.<br /> <br /> The interesting question comes from moral philosophy: Does the changeling still have any claim on their old life if another thinking being is already in possession of it and has lived it for a significant amount of time? Is it okay to try to resume the fetch's relationships even though those people have built such relationships with the fetch instead of the changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if (especially if) the Fetch has made connections and relationships with people the original never even knew?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}